      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An unusual case from our experience of 31 cases with PTCA is presented. In this 59-year-old male patient, partial success of a second PTCA on the restenosed lesion caused almost complete restoration of the coronary artery diameter to its previous size. However, a pressure gradient was still present, in contrast to the initial study where the pressure gradient had decreased satisfactorily. This type of observation is important and needs to be further evaluated."},
